## 1️⃣ Quick-look summary

| Plugin | Works unchanged? | What you must change | Recommended alternative (if you prefer a native MapLibre version) |
|--------|------------------|----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw** | ✅ **Yes** – the library itself works with MapLibre, but you need to rename its CSS class constants (or use the tiny wrapper that does it for you). | • Update the import (`import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw'` → `import MapboxDraw from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-draw'` – same path). <br>• After creating the map, call `new MapboxDraw({ /* options */ })` **exactly the same**. <br>• Replace any hard-coded `mapboxgl-` CSS class names in your own stylesheet (e.g. `.mapboxgl-draw-button`) with the MapLibre equivalents (`.maplibregl-draw-button`). <br>• If you are using the default CSS that ships with the package, import it **after** the MapLibre CSS so the class-name overrides take effect. | • **Terra Draw** – a community-maintained fork that ships a MapLibre-specific CSS file (`terra-draw.css`). Install with `npm i terra-draw terra-draw-maplibre-gl-adapter` and use the same API. |
